@TASK[T004]
GOAL{Define initial rules to prevent semantic drift in a symbolic protocol.}
CTX{Symbolic protocol uses fixed symbols with assigned meanings; drift occurs when symbols acquire unintended interpretations over time.}
PROBLEM{Without constraints, symbols may shift in meaning due to context changes, user reinterpretation, or encoding errors, breaking protocol consistency.}
PLAN{1. Enforce strict symbol-to-meaning mapping with versioned dictionary. 2. Require explicit redefinition for any symbol reuse. 3. Limit symbol scope to defined context. 4. Add checksum or hash for symbol integrity.}
RISK{Over-constraining may reduce flexibility; under-constraining allows drift.}
CHK{Verify mapping uniqueness and scope enforcement in test cases.}
OUT{Rules: (a) One-to-one symbol-meaning binding per protocol version. (b) No implicit overloading. (c) Context boundaries must be declared. (d) Symbol integrity via hash.}
NEXT{Implement rule enforcement in protocol parser; test with drift scenarios.}

